  "details": "Eye movement is ignored when it is counter to head movement.\n\nIf the head is stationary, then eye movement is shown correctly.\n\nIf gaze is fixed on something, and the head moves, then eyes are shown to not move, or barely move relative to the head. Notably eye look blendshapes on avatars that have them are not fired.\n\nThis cannot be an issue with eye tracking hardware or software, as they have no concept of head movement. The cameras will see eye movement relative to headset and send that data.\n\nSo the native VRChat eye tracking is factoring in head movement for some reason, and this is causing it freeze the eyes in place when gaze is fixed.\n\nSee video demonstration here: https://www.reddit.com/r/VRchat/comments/1y4q4c0/native_eye_tracking_issue/",
